#	Revision 3.1  91/07/18  15:40:46  benjamin
#	added HI_RES_CLOCK option, which includes code to initialize a high-res
#	clock (2 microseconds per tick on a 16MHz i386) into the osf1 server's
#	virtual address space, and defines mmap_hi_res_clock to map the clock
#	into the caller's VAS.  It activates the MP_SLAVE_AS_CLK flag in the
#	server compile.  Servers built with this option should only be run on
#	i386 multiprocessor systems, only on top of mach 3.0 microkernels which
#	have also been compiled with the HI_RES_CLOCK option, and only used with
#	emulators which have been modified to permit at least 188 system calls
#	to be recognized (check emulator/i386/emul_machdep.c to be sure).
#	
